0030:     """Rotate each vertical bar's color one slot right and its height one slot left.
0031: 
0032:     Input structure
0033:     - A dominant background surrounds several monochrome one-cell-wide vertical bars.
0034:     - Every bar is bottom-aligned and occupies a distinct column.
0035:     - The ordered bar slots are read from left to right.
0036: 
0037:     Rule
0038:     - Keep the grid shape and the bar columns unchanged.
0039:     - At slot i, use the color from the previous slot cyclically.
0040:     - At slot i, use the height from the next slot cyclically.
0041: 
0042:     Key insight
0043:     - Color and height are independent cyclic attributes of the ordered bar slots:
0044:       colors rotate right while heights rotate left.
0045:     """
0046:     g = np.asarray(grid, dtype=int)
0047:     height = g.shape[0]
0048:     bg = get_bg(g)
0049:     bars = _extract_bars(g, bg)
0050: 
0051:     out = np.full_like(g, bg)
0052:     count = len(bars)
0053:     for i, bar in enumerate(bars):
0054:         color = bars[(i - 1) % count]["color"]
0055:         bar_height = bars[(i + 1) % count]["height"]
0056:         assert 1 <= bar_height <= height
0057:         out[height - bar_height : height, bar["col"]] = color
0058: 
0059:     return out

